1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,145
Yeouido is full of tall buildings. Why is it so flat and straight?

2
00:00:04,145 --> 00:00:09,042
Long ago, it was a sand island in the Han River where the royal family kept sheep and goats.

3
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:13,363
In 1916, an airport was built on this flat sand.

4
00:00:13,363 --> 00:00:17,107
But every rainy season, the whole island went under water.

5
00:00:17,107 --> 00:00:22,293
In 1968, a 7.6 km wall was built around the island in just 110 days.

6
00:00:22,293 --> 00:00:27,046
The stones came from Bamseom, the island next to it. They blew it up with dynamite.

7
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:33,095
In 1971, the runway was gone. It became a big square, and now Yeouido Park.

8
00:00:33,095 --> 00:00:39,000
Where the 333 m Parc1 stands, planes took off 50 years ago.
